WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.870
The Namib Sand Sea: dune after dune, built
of sand carried in from the interior.

2
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:14.390
In Death Valley, on 15 July 1972, the
ground reached 93.9 degrees Celsius,

3
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.210
while the air was 53.3.

4
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:23.350
And in the Sahara, 44 millimetres
of rain once fell in just 3 hours.

5
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.190
Blazing heat, rare but
intense rain, seas of sand.

6
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.050
So where does the sand
in deserts come from?

7
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.970
In this mission, you'll
treat a desert as a system,

8
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.290
driven by energy from the
sun, the wind and rare floods.

9
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.910
Then you'll see how related landforms
combine into a whole landscape.

10
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.520
Your mission: find out where
the sand in deserts comes from.
